agm-0967: AGM H6 charging: polled I2C5 driver and ETA6937 charger setup
(safety 4.40 V / 1.55 A, charge 1.15 A to 4.40 V, input limit 1.5 A,
termination on, PMIC charger_pd cleared), charger watchdog fed every 10 s and
settings re-applied after a chip reset; SweetBattery reports external power,
charging and full from the charger status.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/agm_keys.c b/bsd/dev/agm_keys.c
index 501fecf51..a634033e1 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/agm_keys.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/agm_keys.c
@@ -32,6 +32,20 @@
  * seconds since 1970). The ADI is shared by the input thread, the battery
  * poll and halt/restart, hence agm_adi_lock.
  *
+ * Charger: ETA6937 (bq24157-like) at 0x6a on I2C5 (sprd,sc9860-i2c @0x20210000,
+ * gate AP APB bit 26, clock mux/div at AP clk +0x44, 26 MHz source), driven
+ * polled at 100 kHz like the vendor i2c-sprd.c does with interrupts: reset the
+ * FIFO, ADDR_CFG = addr << 1, COUNT, CTL.MODE (read) / CTL.STP_EN (no stop
+ * before a repeated start), TX bytes, CTL.START, wait for STATUS.INT, then
+ * STATUS.RX_ACK set = NACK. Setup follows eta6937-charger.c hw_init with this
+ * phone's battery node (4.40 V max, 4900 mAh): safety VMREG 4.40 V / IMCHRG
+ * 1.55 A first, charge 1.15 A, VOREG 4.40 V, input limit 2 = 1.5 A (VINDPM
+ * protects weak sources), termination enabled (Linux leaves it to the charger
+ * manager instead), PMIC charger_pd (0x1b98 bit 0) cleared. The chip's 32 s
+ * host watchdog is fed every CHG_POLL_SECS; when it has fallen back to its
+ * defaults (VOREG differs) the setup is applied again. REG0 STAT bits 5:4
+ * (0 ready, 1 charging, 2 done, 3 fault) feed SweetBattery.
+ *
  * Watchdog: the bootloader arms the SC2730 watchdog (base 0x40) for 5 minutes
  * and on Android the CM4 takes it over; the shim reloads it for 40 minutes.
  * Here it is reloaded with AGM_WDT_SECS every AGM_WDT_FEED_SECS, as Linux's
@@ -137,9 +151,47 @@ LCK_SPIN_DECLARE(agm_adi_lock, &agm_lck_grp);
 #define FGU_VOL_1000MV_ADC	691
 #define FGU_CUR_1000MA_ADC	680
 #define RTC			0x200
+#define PMIC_CHGR_PD		0x1b98		/* bit 0: charger disabled */
+#define PMIC_CHGR_DET		0x1ba0
+
+#define I2C_PA			0x20210000UL	/* I2C5 */
+#define I2C_CTL			0x00
+#define I2C_ADDR_CFG		0x04
+#define I2C_COUNT		0x08
+#define I2C_RX			0x0c
+#define I2C_TX			0x10
+#define I2C_STATUS		0x14
+#define I2C_DVD0		0x20
+#define I2C_DVD1		0x24
+#define I2C_STA0_DVD		0x28
+#define I2C_RST			0x2c
+#define I2C_CTL_NACK_EN		(1u << 22)
+#define I2C_CTL_TRANS_EN	(1u << 21)
+#define I2C_CTL_STP_EN		(1u << 20)
+#define I2C_CTL_FULL_INTEN	(1u << 10)
+#define I2C_CTL_EMPTY_INTEN	(1u << 9)
+#define I2C_CTL_DVD_OPT		(1u << 8)
+#define I2C_CTL_MODE		(1u << 3)
+#define I2C_CTL_EN		(1u << 2)
+#define I2C_CTL_INT_EN		(1u << 1)
+#define I2C_CTL_START		(1u << 0)
+#define I2C_ST_INT		(1u << 2)
+#define I2C_ST_RX_ACK		(1u << 1)	/* set: no ACK from the slave */
